From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2_codec2: add VP9 levels 5.1 and 5.2 to the device
 fallback list

"advertise VP9 levels 5.1 and 5.2 by default" extended the fallback list
in DecodeInterface. That list is used only when no decoder device lists
a VP9 input format, or when a device's level control yields no
recognised level. When the driver has no VP9 level control at all,
V4L2Device::queryC2Levels() returns a fallback list of its own, so
DecodeInterface receives that list and does not use its own. The
V4L2Device list still ends at level 5, and applications kept seeing
level 5 as the highest VP9 level of the hardware decoder.

Add levels 5.1 and 5.2 to the V4L2Device list as well, so that both
fallback lists match.

Checked on SC8280XP (Huawei MateBook E Go), whose iris gen1 decoder has
no VP9 level control: MediaCodecInfo now reports level 5.2 for
c2.v4l2.vp9.decoder (level 5 before), and
MediaCodecList.findDecoderForFormat() selects it for 3840x2160 VP9 at
60 fps (level 5.1) and 120 fps (level 5.2), where it returned no
decoder before.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 v4l2/V4L2Device.cpp | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/v4l2/V4L2Device.cpp b/v4l2/V4L2Device.cpp
index 3cf10cf..7b7a134 100644
--- a/v4l2/V4L2Device.cpp
+++ b/v4l2/V4L2Device.cpp
@@ -1662,10 +1662,11 @@ std::vector<C2Config::level_t> V4L2Device::queryC2Levels(uint32_t pixFmt) {
     case V4L2_PIX_FMT_VP9:
     case V4L2_PIX_FMT_VP9_FRAME:
         if (!getSupportedLevels(VideoCodec::VP9, &levels)) {
-            ALOGW("Driver doesn't support QUERY VP9 levels, use default values, 1-5");
+            ALOGW("Driver doesn't support QUERY VP9 levels, use default values, 1-5_2");
             levels = {C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_1,   C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_1_1, C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_2,
                       C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_2_1, C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_3,   C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_3_1,
-                      C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_4,   C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_4_1, C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_5};
+                      C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_4,   C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_4_1, C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_5,
+                      C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_5_1, C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_5_2};
         }
         break;
     case V4L2_PIX_FMT_HEVC:
